ERROR: unknown option: --bogus
Usage: folder_remove_empty [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Remove every empty folder below PATH, deepest first. The start folder itself
is never removed, only the folders below it. Without arguments the window
opens, pre-filled with PATH and the options below.

Options:
  -d, --dryrun     Print the folders that would be removed and remove nothing
  -v, --verbose    Report every kept folder that was left in place
      --no-gui     Work on the terminal instead of opening the window
      --print-man  Print the man page (roff) and exit
      --print-tldr Print the tldr page (markdown) and exit
      --version    Print the program version and exit
  -h, --help       Print this help and exit

Arguments:
  PATH             Folder to scan (default: the current folder)

The window offers the same settings:
  Start path       Folder to scan, checked against the file system as you type;
                   the button behind the field asks for a folder
  Dry run          The option -d
  Verbose          The option -v
  Extra excludes   Folder names that are never removed, ':' separated
  Show in history  Which outcomes the history lists
  Help             Show this text in a dialog that scrolls
  Light/Dark mode  Switch the window between the light and the dark theme
  Exit             Close the window, stopping a run in flight
  Pause            Hold the run in front of the next folder, Resume lets it go
  (Re)start        Start the job, or stop the running one and start it over
  Current folder   The folder that is rated or removed right now
  History          Every folder this session worked on, with its outcome

Kept:
  Never removed: .Trash-1000, .cache, System Volume Information, $RECYCLE.BIN
  (with or without the leading dot), names starting with ZZZZ, names starting
  with four digits and names holding "!!! MISSING !!!" in any letter case.
  Their empty subfolders are still removed, the kept folder itself goes only
  with a parent that is empty apart from empty kept folders.

Environment Variables:
  FOLDER_REMOVE_EMPTY_EXCLUDE   Extra names that are never removed,
                           ':' separated, '*' at the end keeps every name that
                           starts with it

Exit Codes:
  0   The job ran to the end (empty folders removed or listed)
  1   The given PATH does not exist, is not a folder, or an option is unknown
